&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior People Technology Analyst is responsible for leading the design, configuration, and continuous evolution of Workday Human Capital Management (HCM) capabilities as part of SIE’s global People Technology platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role serves as a senior technical leader and functional expert within People Technology Services (PTS), with senior ownership within the Workday Core HCM domain. This role is responsible for system configuration, business process optimization, security administration, custom reporting, and end-user support. Works closely with HR leadership, Payroll, IT, and cross-functional teams to ensure data integrity, streamline employee lifecycle workflows, and maximize the value of the organization’s Workday platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is accountable for ensuring that core HCM solutions are scalable, precise, and aligned with global business requirements, while also contributing to broader Workday platform design and delivery. The role works closely with Human Resources stakeholders to translate policy, regulatory requirements, and business processes into scalable, system-driven solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating within a globally consistent Agile delivery model, this role balances deep domain expertise with cross-platform contribution. The role partners with Product, Integration, Data, and Architecture stakeholders to deliver cohesive, end-to-end solutions and to establish sustainable configuration patterns across the platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is suited for individuals who combine deep expertise in Workday HCM with strong systems thinking, technical leadership, and the ability to influence design decisions across a global platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain Ownership &amp;amp; Platform Leadership (Core HCM)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior functional and technical lead for the Workday Core HCM domain, leading complex configuration design, system enhancements, and ongoing platform evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and implementation of complex Core HCM solutions in partnership with Human Resources stakeholders, ensuring alignment with business requirements, global standards, regulatory requirements, and operational needs:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and maintain core Workday HCM components, including supervisory organizations, job families, positions, location hierarchies, and worker profiles. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and optimize Workday Business Processes (BPs) (e.g., Hire, Transfer, Promote, Terminate, Job Change) using condition rules and validation logic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage domain and business process security policies, ensuring appropriate role-based access control and data privacy compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce configuration design patterns that ensure scalability, reusability, and maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key technical authority for Core HCM design decisions, guiding trade-offs between business requirements, system capabilities, and long-term platform sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure alignment of HCM and core configurations with global policies, regulatory requirements, and downstream dependencies (e.g., payroll)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solution Design &amp;amp; Delivery Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Human Resources stakeholders to clarify requirements, challenge assumptions, and guide toward scalable, platform-aligned solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end delivery of complex Workday HCM related initiatives, including design, build, testing, and deployment readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex business rules, policies, and regulatory requirements into structured, scalable system configurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership across workstreams, ensuring consistency and quality of solutions delivered by the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and guide analysts in solution design and configuration, ensuring alignment with platform standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Engineering &amp;amp; Cross-Domain Contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to broader Workday platform design and configuration across additional domains (e.g., Absence &amp;amp; Leave, Compensation, Talent, Performance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Integration and Data specialists to ensure end-to-end solution integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in platform-level design discussions, influencing architecture, standards, and ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure solutions integrate effectively with upstream and downstream systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data, Reporting &amp;amp; Downstream Integrity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and oversee reporting solutions and calculated fields supporting core HCM and related processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Workday HCM core data supports HR reporting, compliance, and downstream processes (e.g., payroll and analytics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data accuracy, integrity, and consistency across Workday configurations and downstream consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Reliability &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure reliability and stability of business processes through proactive issue identification and root cause resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify systemic issues and drive structural improvements to platform design and configuration practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives to simplify, standardize, and continuously improve Core HCM configurations, business processes, and data structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to evolving platform standards, governance models, and configuration frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance, Compliance &amp;amp; Standards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure adherence to global PTS design standards, governance practices, and engineering principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure core HCM configurations meet data privacy, security, and audit requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to documentation standards, testing practices, and release management processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience with enterprise platforms, including significant hands-on experience with Workday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in designing and implementing core HCM solutions, eligibility rules, calculated fields and business processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to own and lead complex configuration domains, including defining design patterns and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of core HCM related business processes across multiple regions and regulatory contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate complex business rules and policies into scalable, maintainable system configurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to troubleshoot and resolve complex configuration issues, including calculation logic and system behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience developing Workday reports and Workday Security configuration &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with mass data uploads using Enterprise Interface Builder (EIB) tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple Workday domains and understanding cross-domain dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to guide and mentor other analysts in solution design and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payroll processes and downstream integrations &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to integrations (e.g., EIB, Core Connectors) or inbound/outbound payroll feeds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to platform architecture, standards, or governance frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in global, matrixed enterprise environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profile:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in Workday Core HCM, with the ability to lead complex solution and configuration design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems thinker who understands cross-domain dependencies, downstream impacts, and the broader People Technology ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at translating complex or ambiguous business requirements, policies, and regulations into scalable, sustainable system solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operates as a senior technical leader who guides others, influences design decisions, and remains hands-on when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trusted partner to Human Resources stakeholders, with strong consulting, communication, and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates strong ownership, sound judgment, and a consistent focus on data integrity, platform reliability, and high-quality outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a global, evolving environment, with the ability to influence beyond immediate responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
